<title>FINLAND: JUSTICE CHANCELLOR INVESTIGATES ALHO ERM ACTIONS.</title>
<headline>JUSTICE CHANCELLOR INVESTIGATES ALHO ERM ACTIONS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chancellor of Justice Jorma Aalto said on Monday he had started a preliminary investigation of second Finance Minister Arja Alho's actions on October 12 when the decision was made to peg the markka to the ERM.</p>
<p>The chancellor's office said in a statement that Bank of Finland supervisors Olavi Ala-Nissila, Anneli Jaatteenmaki and Mauri Pekkarinen -- all of the centre party -- had informed the chancellor that Alho may have revealed the Finnish negotiators' &quot;authorisation limits&quot; to the counterparty.</p>
<p>Aalto had asked Bank of Finland and finance ministry officials to give information about the case by October 28.</p>
<p>&quot;When the reports have arrived and been examined, the chancellor will assess the need for further action,&quot; the office said.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 89 6805 0247</p>
